From: GetLine maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] close VpnService fd on sing_tun.New error before tunNew

Parent-tracked patch for the clash-foss (Mihomo) submodule.
Applied after `git submodule update` by scripts/apply-mihomo-patches.sh
(and core Gradle Golang build). Do not rely on a dirty submodule working tree.

Upstream gitlink remains MetaCubeX/mihomo @ recorded SHA; this product
change is intentionally not pushed to upstream.

Android VpnService passes a FileDescriptor into sing_tun.New. Errors before
tunNew (NewListenerHandler, buildAndroidRules / package manager) returned
without closing it: Listener.Close sees tunIf == nil. Later errors after
tunNew already close the fd via tunIf, so a blanket close on every New
error is a double-close race.

This guard closes the raw fd only until tunNew takes it.

Applies with: git -C core/src/foss/golang/clash apply -p1 < this file
(or via scripts/apply-mihomo-patches.sh)

---
diff --git a/listener/sing_tun/server.go b/listener/sing_tun/server.go
index 3e5ef591..fa3f05b4 100644
--- a/listener/sing_tun/server.go
+++ b/listener/sing_tun/server.go
@@ -134,6 +134,14 @@ func checkTunName(tunName string) (ok bool) {
 }
 
 func New(options LC.Tun, tunnel C.Tunnel, additions ...inbound.Addition) (l *Listener, err error) {
+	tunFd := options.FileDescriptor
+	tunFdReleased := false
+	defer func() {
+		if err != nil && !tunFdReleased && tunFd > 0 {
+			_ = os.NewFile(uintptr(tunFd), "tun").Close()
+		}
+	}()
+
 	if len(additions) == 0 {
 		additions = []inbound.Addition{
 			inbound.WithInName("DEFAULT-TUN"),
@@ -480,6 +488,7 @@ func New(options LC.Tun, tunnel C.Tunnel, additions ...inbound.Addition) (l *Lis
 		err = E.Cause(err, "configure tun interface")
 		return
 	}
+	tunFdReleased = true
 
 	l.dnsServerIp = dnsServerIp
 	// after tun.New sing-tun has set DNS to TUN interface
